# GPU-fit tuning: Qwen3.8-27B instruct/non-thinking on 2x R9700.
#
# models/qwen3.8-27b-instruct.env uses the same UD-Q8_K_XL weights as
# models/qwen3.8-27b-q8.env, so the memory budget is identical -- see
# profiles/r9700-dual/qwen3.8-27b-q8.env for the full breakdown
# (~40 GiB of ~62 GiB at 262K, ~22 GiB slack).
#
# This file exists so the instruct config does not silently fall back to the
# card-generic 32K default in profiles/r9700-dual/default.env.
#
# Note that non-thinking mode does not need the huge reasoning budget the
# thinking config does (upstream budgets reasoning at up to 262,144 tokens and
# the final response at 131,072). The native context is still what it is, so it
# costs nothing to keep it -- but if you want the slack for concurrency
# instead, PARALLEL=2 with CTX_SIZE=131072 is a better shape for instruct
# serving than one idle 262K slot.
: "${CTX_SIZE:=262144}"
: "${UBATCH:=512}"

# --- split mode ----------------------------------------------------------
# Same dense-model reasoning as profiles/r9700-dual/qwen3.8-27b-q8.env, where
# this was measured (row: +32.8% prefill, +9.5% decode over layer, and it
# fixes the GPU[0]-at-97% VRAM imbalance). Measured on the Q8 weights, not
# these, but the cause is architectural -- a dense model idles one card under
# `layer` regardless of quant. Set SPLIT_MODE=layer inline to A/B it back.
: "${SPLIT_MODE:=row}"

# --- vision disabled on this host ----------------------------------------
# The model envs pass --mmproj (the model is natively VL). This host does not
# use it, and the projector costs ~0.86 GiB on the PRIMARY card -- which here
# is also the card driving the displays, and the one that runs out of VRAM
# first (it carries the KV cache and compute buffers on top of its weight
# share). --no-mmproj overrides the earlier --mmproj; verified against this
# image's llama-server, which loads text-only with both flags present.
#
# Machine-level, not model-level, ON PURPOSE: models/qwen3.8-27b*.env are
# shared with strixhalo, which has ~46 GiB spare and no reason to give up
# vision. Delete this line to re-enable images/video here.
LLAMA_ARGS+=(--no-mmproj)

# --- weight split, biased off the display card ---------------------------
# UNEVEN ON PURPOSE. --tensor-split redistributes WEIGHTS ONLY; the KV cache
# and compute buffers always land on the primary card, so an even "1,1" split
# leaves the two cards badly lopsided. Measured on the Q8 config at 262K
# before this change: card0 32,479 of 32,624 MiB used (145 MiB free) vs card1
# 20,380 MiB (11.9 GiB free) -- a ~11.8 GiB gap, of which only the weight half
# is tunable here.
#
# On THIS host the primary card also drives two displays (DRM card1 =
# PCI 03:00.0 = ROCm GPU[0]; the DRM and ROCm numbering are INVERTED, so check
# `rocm-smi --showbus` against /sys/class/drm/*/status before re-tuning). The
# compositor and browser allocate from that same pool at unpredictable times,
# so it wants the LARGER reserve, not an equal one.
#
# Projected for Q8 @ 262K with --no-mmproj (weights 29.3 GiB, KV 8.5 GiB):
#   1,1      card0 30.8 GiB / 1.0 free   card1 19.9 GiB / 12.0 free
#   0.65,1.35  card0 25.7 / 6.2 free     card1 25.0 / 6.8 free   (equal free)
#   0.6,1.4    card0 25.0 / 6.9 free     card1 25.8 / 6.1 free   <- chosen
# 0.6,1.4 is one notch past the equal-free point, deliberately favouring the
# display card. The BF16 and instruct configs share this ratio; their weight
# totals differ, so the absolute figures shift but the bias direction holds.
#
# These are projections from measured non-weight load, NOT a measured load.
# Verify with `rocm-smi --showmemuse` after starting the server, and if card0
# is still tight go to 0.55,1.45 before cutting CTX_SIZE.
TENSOR_SPLIT="${TENSOR_SPLIT:-0.6,1.4}"
